    <article class="card doc-content prose">
      <div class="kicker">Getting started</div>
      <h1>Deploy your first package</h1>
      <p class="lead">A minimal path to â€œhello worldâ€ on BASRUN (static placeholder).</p>

      <h2>1) Write a Basil file</h2>
      <div class="codeblock" style="margin-top: 10px;">
        <header><span>main.basil</span><span class="kbd">scheduled</span></header>
        <pre><code>fn run():
  log.info("Hello from BASRUN")
  return 0</code></pre>
      </div>

      <h2>2) Create a package</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Upload `main.basil` (or a ZIP)</li>
        <li>Select a mode: Scheduled / Webhook / REST</li>
        <li>Choose the entry point (for example `main.basil`)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3) Run it</h2>
      <p>In scheduled mode you configure a cron expression. In webhook mode you call the generated URL. In REST mode you call endpoints under a base path.</p>

      <div class="callout" style="margin-top: 14px;">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> Use the <a href="../app/dashboard.basil">dashboard mock</a> to preview the intended flow.
      </div>
    </article>
